            <div xml:id="d1071">

                <pb facs="0835" n="753" xml:id="pg753"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 431.11 Or 4/172</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The American Chargé d’Affaires to the Secretary of
                        State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Caracas</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1910-12-20"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">December 20, 1910</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 640.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose herewith a
                    check, drawn on Messrs. G. Amsinck &amp; Co., New York, by the Bank of
                    Venezuela, for sixty-four thousand four hundred and twelve dollars fifty-nine
                    cents ($64,412.59) in payment of the award of The Hague Tribunal in the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Orinoco</hi> steamship case.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sheldon
                    Whitehouse.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
